  "Question": "If \\(i^2=-1,\\) then \\((1+i)^{20}-(1-i)^{20}\\) equals",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-1024\\)",
    "B": "\\(-1024i\\)",
    "C": "\\(0\\)",
    "D": "\\(1024\\)",
    "E": "\\(1024i\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "Since \\(20=4\\cdot5\\), finding the fourth powers lets us avoid expanding twentieth powers. Using \\(i^2=-1\\),\n\\[\n(1+i)^2=1+2i+i^2=2i,\n\\qquad\n(1-i)^2=1-2i+i^2=-2i.\n\\]\nSquaring again gives\n\\[\n(1+i)^4=(2i)^2=-4,\n\\qquad\n(1-i)^4=(-2i)^2=-4.\n\\]\nThus both twentieth powers equal \\((-4)^5=-1024\\). Their difference is therefore \\(0\\), choice C.",
